    <li>From a reaction of S + O<sub>2</sub> -&gt; SO<sub>2</sub> we&rsquo;re able to determine that the limiting reactant would be sulfur because the amount of O<sub>2</sub> in the air is higher than the amount of sulfur that is burned in the reaction.</li>
